.TH SOCKET 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Library Reference"
.SH NAME
Socket \- low-level Berkeley socket networking
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B Socket
module provides low-level TCP/UDP socket programming via the POSIX Berkeley
socket API.
.PP
Constants: AF_INET, AF_INET6, SOCK_STREAM, SOCK_DGRAM, SOCK_RAW,
IPPROTO_TCP, IPPROTO_UDP, SOL_SOCKET, SO_REUSEADDR, SO_BROADCAST.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS create
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
SocketObj() Socket.create(domain: int(), type: int(), protocol: int())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Creates a socket.  Returns a SocketObj instance.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR, \fBRuntimeError\fR
.SH "SOCKETOBJ METHODS"
.TP
\fBbind(host, port)\fR
Bind to host:port (AF_INET/dotted-decimal).
Raises \fBRuntimeError\fR on failure.
.TP
\fBlisten(backlog)\fR
Mark as passive server socket with given backlog.
Raises \fBRuntimeError\fR on failure.
.TP
\fBaccept()\fR -> SocketObj()
Accept a pending connection; blocks until a client connects.
Raises \fBRuntimeError\fR on failure.
.TP
\fBconnect(host, port)\fR
Connect to remote host:port.
Raises \fBRuntimeError\fR on failure.
.TP
\fBsend(data)\fR -> int()
Send data string; returns bytes sent.
.TP
\fBrecv(size)\fR -> string()
Receive up to size bytes; returns empty string on closed connection.
.TP
\fBclose()\fR
Close the socket.
.TP
\fBsetblocking(bool)\fR
Set blocking (true) or non-blocking (false) mode.
.TP
\fBsetsockopt(level, optname, value)\fR
Set a socket option.
Raises \fBRuntimeError\fR on failure.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
Http(3), Serial(3)
